  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Burnham gambles on radical progressive plan to help Britain ‘rise again’",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/sep/29/andy-burnham-vows-long-term-relationship-eu-labour-conference-speech",
      "description": "<p>PM accepts some of his plan could be difficult and admits he ‘may pay a political price’</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/sep/29/burnhams-emotional-solo-act-had-labour-in-raptures-but-his-promises-will-take-time-to-come-good\">Analysis: PM’s promises will take time to come good</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/sep/29/brexit-electoral-reform-key-takeaways-andy-burnham-conference-speech\">Key takeaways from Burnham’s conference speech</a></p></li></ul><p>Andy Burnham has staked his future on a gamble that the public will back radical progressive policies on social care, electoral reform and Europe, telling voters that his agenda will break the mould of the last 40 years and “allow us to rise again”.</p><p>In a deeply personal speech at Labour’s conference, Burnham began building his next general election manifesto, acknowledging that he may end up paying the price for creating sharp new dividing lines in politics.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/sep/29/andy-burnham-vows-long-term-relationship-eu-labour-conference-speech\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-29T18:21:29"
    },
    {
      "title": "Burnham’s emotional solo act had Labour in raptures – but his promises will take time to come good",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/sep/29/burnhams-emotional-solo-act-had-labour-in-raptures-but-his-promises-will-take-time-to-come-good",
      "description": "<p>PM’s speech, written almost entirely alone, was full of radicalism but his biggest plans will have to wait until after the next election</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/sep/29/brexit-electoral-reform-key-takeaways-andy-burnham-conference-speech\">Key takeaways from Andy Burnham’s conference speech</a></p></li></ul><p>Hope Again is the conference slogan. But what felt even more apt was Try Again.</p><p>Just forget about the last two years, after the party won a historic majority but where the mood never matched the achievement. Now, as conference delegates and MPs filed out of the hall after Andy <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/sep/29/andy-burnham-vows-long-term-relationship-eu-labour-conference-speech\">Burnham’s first speech as prime minister</a>, it was close to euphoria. Where the hell have you been all our lives? What have we been doing – when you were right there all along?</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/sep/29/burnhams-emotional-solo-act-had-labour-in-raptures-but-his-promises-will-take-time-to-come-good\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-29T17:13:39"
    },
